DeepFilterNet 3. The app downloads DeepFilterNet3_onnx.tar.gz (SHA-256
c94d91f70911001c946e0fabb4aa9adc37045f45a03b56008cb0c8244cb63616) from the DeepFilterNet
repository at tag v0.5.6 (https://github.com/Rikorose/DeepFilterNet, models/), or from the
jsDelivr mirror of the same tag. The file is part of that repository, which is licensed
under MIT OR Apache-2.0 (LICENSE, LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE at its root; Copyright (c)
2021 Hendrik Schröter). The repository does not give the model a separate license.
DeepFilterNet 3 is described in Schröter et al., "DeepFilterNet: Perceptually Motivated
Real-Time Speech Enhancement" (https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.08227).

NVIDIA Real-time RE-USE. The app downloads NVIDIA Real-time RE-USE weights
(model.safetensors, revision 4c0c186) from https://huggingface.co/alshell7/hush-ai or
https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Real-time_RE-USE.
They are licensed by NVIDIA under the NVIDIA One-Way Noncommercial License
(https://github.com/NVlabs/HMAR/blob/main/LICENSE): non-commercial research and
educational use only. The app shows this license and asks the user to accept it before
the download.

The sample recording in site/public/samples (noisy.mp3) comes from the same NVIDIA
repository, and hush.mp3 is that recording processed by Hush AI. Both are under the
NVIDIA One-Way Noncommercial License; see site/public/samples/LICENSE.

